###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Mean wall-clock time per optimisation evaluation on a single T4 GPU:
# about 32.4 minutes (QM9), 9.6 (rMD17 aspirin), 6.0 (rMD17 benzene) and
# 4.8 (Cu-Li); recorded as text in trainingHardware.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The +MLP and +QDI models are modifications of Allegro's output pathway and are encoded under entity:Allegro with a 'variant' setting (METHODS.md rule 3). The QDI layer is a quantum-circuit layer; whether it ran on a simulator or on hardware was not captured.
# - Errors are validation MAEs of the best runs (up to 300 epochs for QM9, 100 for Cu-Li, 3000 for aspirin and benzene), not test errors. The Cu-Li energy MAEs (809.0 / 698.9 / 495.7 meV/atom) are as printed and are strikingly large.
# - Tuned hyperparameters are encoded for baseline Allegro and Allegro+MLP (Tables I and II: r_max as cutoffRadius, learning rate, batch size, layers); the polynomial cutoff P and the MLP widths are left out, and Table III (Allegro+QDI) was not read.
# - The column 'Allegro [12]' of Tables IV and V and the comparison Table VI are literature values. The reference levels of rMD17 and QM9 are not restated.
# - The venue string in the manifest ('Jyvaskyla University Digital Archive') is the repository; the DOI is that of Computational Materials Science. The manifest notes that the DOI had to be cleaned.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

